# ── fleet API credentials — THIS REPO IS PUBLIC ──────────────
# 10 untracked files were found holding 30 LIVE keys (Groq gsk_, NVIDIA NIM
# nvapi-, SambaNova) — verified live against the providers, HTTP 200. None had
# ever been committed; one `git add -A` would have published all of them.
#
# 🔴 THE NEAR-MISS THAT ALLOWED IT: the list already had `*.key`, which does
# NOT match `key.txt`. A pattern that looks like it covers credentials and
# misses by one character is worse than no pattern, because nobody looks twice.
# These match by BASENAME (no leading path) so they apply at any depth — a new
# game's fleet folder is covered before it exists.
key.txt
keys.json
*_keys.json
*_key.txt
api_key*
# the workers read these at runtime, so they stay ON DISK and only stay OUT of git
games/*/fleet/**/key*
games/*/fleet/**/*key*.json

# ── scratch working directory — THIS REPO IS PUBLIC ──────────
# 1,110 of the files git was about to add came from two CHROME PROFILES left
# behind by the PDF-export scripts: Login Data (saved passwords), Web Data
# (autofill: names, addresses, phone numbers), History, and a Local State
# holding os_crypt.encrypted_key — the master key those databases are sealed
# with. DPAPI ties it to this Windows account, so it is not remotely
# decryptable, but browsing history and autofill are plain SQLite and none of
# it is ours to publish. Nothing under scratchpad/ has ever been tracked.
scratchpad/

# ── oversized derived data — GitHub REJECTS a file over 100 MB ───
# 25 files over 50 MB were about to be pushed, 13 of them over the hard limit,
# which fails the ENTIRE push rather than skipping the file.
#
# 🔴 THE SAME NEAR-MISS AS THE KEYS: the list already had `games/*/work/*.json`
# and `games/*/work/*.xml`, and a single `*` does not descend. Every offender
# sat one level deeper - work/_fontinspect/, work/fontwork/, fleet/. `**` is
# what those rules meant all along.
#
# None of this is source: font-inspection dumps, extraction spines and fleet
# corpora are all re-derivable from the game plus the fleet, and they churn
# constantly - the worst possible shape for git. They live on Drive instead.
games/*/work/**/*.json
games/*/work/**/*.xml
games/*/work/**/*.bin
games/*/work/**/*_full.txt
games/*/fleet/**/*corpus*.json
games/*/fleet/**/onscreens_panel.json
games/*/fleet/**/newera_cc.json
games/*/*dualgender*.json
# vendor installers - re-downloadable from the vendor, never ours to publish
*.msi
# pre-<milestone> sidecars: a snapshot taken before a big re-run, same size as
# the corpus it shadows and never source.
*.pre_newera
*.pre_*

# ── per-game DATA — git carries the source, Drive carries the data ──
# Measured on the first push in 7.5 weeks: 6,413 new files, 1,555 MB.
# 2,546 of them were source (.py/.md/.cs/…) and weighed 25.7 MB. The other
# 3,867 were 1,530 MB of derived data - corpora, extracted fonts, sprites,
# game containers, vendored .jars. That is 98.3% of the bytes for 1.7% of the
# meaning, in a repo we had just cut from 308 GB to 276 MB.
#
# These are re-derivable (from the game, or from a fleet re-run) and they churn
# on every run, so git stores a fresh full copy each time - the exact shape that
# made this repo unpushable in June. The bulk lives on Drive; git keeps what
# a human wrote. Scoped to games/ so the app's own assets are unaffected.
games/**/*.json
games/**/*.jsonl
games/**/*.ttf
games/**/*.otf
games/**/*.png
games/**/*.jpg
games/**/*.dds
games/**/*.gfx
games/**/*.dpc
games/**/*.forge
games/**/*.psarc
games/**/*.prev
games/**/*.jar
games/**/*.pdf
games/**/*.ld
games/**/*.bak-*
games/**/*.pre_*

# ── games/ is DATA by default, source by exception ───────────
# Chasing data extensions one at a time never converged (json -> pak -> tgz ->
# oiv -> w3strings -> locres -> xpps ...), because every game brings its own
# container format. Inverting it does: under games/ the DEFAULT is "not in
# git", and the exceptions are the file types a person actually writes.
# Already-tracked files are unaffected - an ignore rule never untracks.
games/**
!games/**/
!games/**/*.py
!games/**/*.md
!games/**/*.sh
!games/**/*.bat
!games/**/*.ps1
!games/**/*.cs
!games/**/*.ts
!games/**/*.yml
!games/**/*.yaml
!games/**/*.toml
!games/**/*.ini

# ── stragglers found by measuring the push set ─────────────
# The list already had *.bak.* and *.bak[0-9]* — but the requeue scripts write
# the DASH form, so the biggest single leftover slipped through both.
*.bak-*
# vendored OCR language data (tesseract) — re-downloadable, not our source
*.traineddata
_tessdata/
# fleet/QA checkpoints: run state, rewritten continuously, meaningless to a reader
universal/*checkpoint*.json
universal/cross_audit_flags_*.json
